Repo: `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa`. Branch: `feature/SFCC-831-689_country-language-mismatch`. Steps A1/A2 already committed. Step B1 is implemented but NOT yet committed — a human visual check found a real defect. This is a REWORK round on Step B1, not a new step.

## The defect, confirmed by direct measurement, not guesswork

`ZimmCountryLanguageMismatch` uses `ZimmDrawer`'s `labelledBy=` form (correct — this design has no title row). But `ZimmDrawer`'s close button, in that form, floats via `position: absolute` at `top: var(--zimm-scale-3xl)` (40px) with `height: DRAWER_HEADER_ROW_HEIGHT` (44px) — occupying the vertical band **y=40px to y=84px** from the panel's top edge (`overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmDrawer/zimmDrawer.css.ts:123-130`, `zimmDrawerShared.ts`). Nothing reserves this space automatically for a `labelledBy=` consumer — that only happens for the `title=` form, via a dedicated header row.

`zimmCountryLanguageMismatch.css.ts`'s `root.padding: var(--zimm-scale-xl)` (24px, uniform) was copied from `zimmAuthDrawerContent.css.ts` as the nearest precedent — but that component uses `title=`, so it has never faced this problem at all; it was the wrong reference for this specific question. With 24px top padding, a 16px heading line-height (`heading3`), and a 16px gap, the body paragraph starts at approximately y=58px — inside the close button's 40–84px band. Confirmed visually by Marcel: the close icon renders overlapping the body text on both variants (screenshots showed the × sitting mid-sentence in the wrapped paragraph, not in a clear top-right corner).

## The fix

In `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmCountryLanguageMismatch/zimmCountryLanguageMismatch.css.ts`:

1. Add a new constant, near the top of the file alongside any other file-level constants (or inline if the file has none yet — check its current structure first):

```ts
// SFCC-831 — this component uses ZimmDrawer's `labelledBy` form (floating close button), not
// `title` (reserved header row) — so unlike zimmAuthDrawerContent (which uses `title` and gets
// the close button's clearance for free via ZimmDrawer's own header row), nothing pushes this
// component's own content below the close button's footprint. The close button occupies
// y=40px (INSET_COMPACT.top, zimmDrawer.css.ts:57) to y=84px (+ DRAWER_HEADER_ROW_HEIGHT, 44px,
// zimmDrawerShared.ts) from the panel's top edge, at every breakpoint (this component's `prompt`
// drawer size has no closeButton override of its own, so it inherits baseStyle's INSET_COMPACT
// unchanged — confirm this is still true before relying on this comment). Root's own top padding
// must clear that or the close button visually overlaps the heading/body text — confirmed via a
// real visual check, both variants, SFCC-831.
// audit-allow: provisional — derived from ZimmDrawer's own closeButton geometry via file
// citation, not re-exported as a shared constant; revisit if INSET_COMPACT.top or
// DRAWER_HEADER_ROW_HEIGHT ever change, since this value would silently go stale.
const CLOSE_BUTTON_CLEARANCE = '5.25rem'; // 84px = 40px (INSET_COMPACT.top) + 44px (DRAWER_HEADER_ROW_HEIGHT)
```

2. In the `root` part, keep `padding: 'var(--zimm-scale-xl)'` (uniform 24px — already visually confirmed correct on the other three sides), and add `paddingTop: CLOSE_BUTTON_CLEARANCE` as a separate property **after** `padding` in the object (so it overrides just the top side; object key order matters for this to work — `padding` sets all four sides, then the later `paddingTop` key overrides only that one side).

**Before you make this change**, independently verify the two numbers this fix depends on by reading the actual current files yourself — don't take my citation on faith:
- `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmDrawer/zimmDrawer.css.ts` — confirm `INSET_COMPACT`'s `top` value and `closeButton`'s `height` value.
- Confirm the `prompt` variant (added in Step A1) has no `closeButton` override of its own, so it genuinely inherits `baseStyle.closeButton` unchanged at every breakpoint — if this has changed since A1, the 84px figure may be wrong and you need to recompute it, not apply it blindly.
- Confirm `heading3`'s actual line-height and the `content` part's actual gap value, to sanity-check that 84px genuinely clears the close button with the real heading text (not just my arithmetic above).

## After the fix

1. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run test` (full suite) — expect the same 78 files / 1182 tests / 0 failures as before (this is a value-only recipe change, no new test should be needed, but if you believe a new one is warranted to prevent this exact regression, say so in your report rather than silently adding one).
2. Run `npm run audit:tokens` — the new `CLOSE_BUTTON_CLEARANCE` constant must be correctly acknowledged (it already carries the `audit-allow:` comment above) — confirm the count is still exactly 3 unacknowledged, not 4.
3. **Start Storybook if it isn't already running** (`npm run storybook` — check if port 6006 is already serving first) and take a screenshot or otherwise directly inspect the rendered `Layout/ZimmCountryLanguageMismatch` → `Location` and `Language` stories yourself to confirm the close button no longer overlaps any text, at both variants. Don't just trust the arithmetic — look at the actual result, the same way the defect was originally caught by looking.

**Do not touch anything else** — not `zimmDrawer.css.ts`, not `zimmDrawerShared.ts`, not any other file. This fix is entirely contained to `zimmCountryLanguageMismatch.css.ts`.

Report back: the exact change made, your own independent verification of the two numbers before applying the fix, the tsc/test/audit numbers, and — most importantly — what you actually saw when you looked at the rendered result.

